+--------------------------------+

log canonical threshold of a generic determinantal ideal
========================================================

  * Usage: 
        multiplierIdeal(L,r)
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, dimensions $\{m,n\}$ of a matrix
      * r, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the size of minors generating
        the determinantal ideal
  * Outputs:
      * a *note rational number: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,, 
Computes the log canonical threshold of the ideal of $r \times r$ minors in a
$m \times n$ matrix whose entries are independent variables (a generic matrix).

lct of ideal of 2-by-2 minors of 4-by-5 matrix:

+--------------------------------+
|i20 : x = getSymbol "x";        |
+--------------------------------+
|i21 : R = QQ[x_1..x_20];        |
+--------------------------------+
|i22 : X = genericMatrix(R,4,5); |
|                                |
|              4      5          |
|o22 : Matrix R  <-- R           |
+--------------------------------+
|i23 : logCanonicalThreshold(X,2)|
|                                |
|o23 = 10                        |
|                                |
|o23 : QQ                        |
+--------------------------------+
We produce some tables of lcts:
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i24 :                                                          |
|            lctTable = (M,N,r) -> (                            |
|              x = getSymbol "x";                               |
|              R := QQ[x_1..x_(M*N)];                           |
|              netList (                                        |
|              prepend( join({"m\\n"}, toList(3..M)),           |
|              for n from 3 to N list (                         |
|                prepend(n,                                     |
|                for m from 3 to min(n,M) list (                |
|                  logCanonicalThreshold(genericMatrix(R,m,n),r)|
|                ))                                             |
|              ))                                               |
|            ));                                                |
