multiplierIdeal(MonomialIdeal,QQ) -- multiplier ideal
*****************************************************

  * Function: *note multiplierIdeal:
    (HyperplaneArrangements)multiplierIdeal_lpQQ_cmCentralArrangement_cmList_rp
    ,

Description
===========

multiplier ideal of a monomial ideal
====================================

  * Usage: 
        multiplierIdeal(I,t)
  * Inputs:
      * I, a *note monomial ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)MonomialIdeal,, a monomial
        ideal in a polynomial ring
      * t, a *note rational number: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,, a coefficient
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
Computes the multiplier ideal of $I$ with coefficient $t$ using Howald's
Theorem and the package *note Normaliz: (Normaliz)Top,.
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y];                                             |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = monomialIdeal(y^2,x^3);                              |
|                                                              |
|o2 : MonomialIdeal of R                                       |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : multiplierIdeal(I,5/6)                                   |
|                                                              |
|o3 = monomialIdeal (x, y)                                     |
|                                                              |
|o3 : MonomialIdeal of R                                       |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : J = monomialIdeal(x^8,y^6); -- Example 2 of [Howald 2000]|
|                                                              |
|o4 : MonomialIdeal of R                                       |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : multiplierIdeal(J,1)                                     |
|                                                              |
|                     6   5    4 2   2 3     4   5             |
|o5 = monomialIdeal (x , x y, x y , x y , x*y , y )            |
|                                                              |
|o5 : MonomialIdeal of R                                       |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

multiplier ideal of a hyperplane arrangement
============================================

  * Usage: 
        multiplierIdeal(A,m,s)
  * Inputs:
      * A, a *note central hyperplane arrangement:
        (HyperplaneArrangements)CentralArrangement,, a central hyperplane
        arrangement
      * m, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of weights for the
        hyperplanes in $A$ (optional)
      * s, a *note number: (Macaulay2Doc)Number,, a coefficient
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
Computes the multiplier ideal of the ideal of $A$ with coefficient $s$ using
the package *note HyperplaneArrangements: (HyperplaneArrangements)Top,.
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                                                   |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : f = toList factor((x^2 - y^2)*(x^2 - z^2)*(y^2 - z^2)*z) / first;|
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : A = arrangement f;                                               |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : multiplierIdeal(A,3/7)                                           |
|                                                                      |
|o9 = ideal (z, y, x)                                                  |
|                                                                      |
|o9 : Ideal of R                                                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------+

multiplier ideal of monomial space curve
========================================

  * Usage: 
        I = multiplierIdeal(R,n,t)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,
      * n, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of three integers
      * t, a *note rational number: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,
  * Outputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,

Computes the multiplier ideal of the space curve $C$ parametrized by
$(t^a,t^b,t^c)$ given by $n=(a,b,c)$.

+--------------------------------+
|i10 : R = QQ[x,y,z];            |
+--------------------------------+
|i11 : n = {2,3,4};              |
+--------------------------------+
|i12 : t = 5/2;                  |
+--------------------------------+
|i13 : I = multiplierIdeal(R,n,t)|
|                                |
|              2         2       |
|o13 = ideal (y  - x*z, x  - z)  |
|                                |
|o13 : Ideal of R                |
+--------------------------------+

multiplier ideal of a generic determinantal ideal
=================================================

  * Usage: 
        multiplierIdeal(R,L,r,t)
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, a ring
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, dimensions $\{m,n\}$ of a matrix
      * r, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the size of minors generating
        the determinantal ideal
      * t, a *note rational number: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,, a coefficient
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
Computes the multiplier ideal of the ideal of $r \times r$ minors in a $m
\times n$ matrix whose entries are independent variables in the ring $R$ (a
generic matrix).
+-------------------------------+
|i14 : x = symbol x;            |
+-------------------------------+
|i15 : R = QQ[x_1..x_20];       |
+-------------------------------+
|i16 : X = genericMatrix(R,4,5);|
|                               |
|              4      5         |
|o16 : Matrix R  <-- R          |
+-------------------------------+
|i17 : multiplierIdeal(X,2,5/7) |
|                               |
|o17 = ideal 1                  |
|                               |
|o17 : Ideal of R               |
+-------------------------------+

